\section{\texttt{glob.iglob} is a generator}

\begin{note}
\texttt{glob.iglob} accepts exactly the same parameters as \texttt{glob.glob},
but returns an iterator instead of a list.
The set of matches is identical; only the type is different.
An iterator supports \texttt{next} but not \texttt{len} and not indexing,
and it is consumed as you read it.
Therefore calling \texttt{list} on the same iterator twice
gives a full list followed by an empty list.
\end{note}
